A1. Putting two and two together—this is the pastime of the younger generation. ~ NECKING
A7. Fiction depicts numerous lovers of this type. ~ DASHING
A13. A moving filling-station. ~ DINER
A14. You can't do this when you "pass out." ~ ENTER
A15. There are several of these in "error." ~ RR
A17. A God of Nature in Hindoo mythology. ~ DEVA
A18. The length of a lover's promise. ~ EVER
A19. This comes before noon. (Abbr.) ~ AM
A20. A human sponge. ~ SOT
A22. A speedy quadruped. (A name.) ~ ZEV
A23. This dwells in fruity surroundings. ~ PIT
A24. A lugubrious sisterhood. ~ SOB
A25. A man's name. ~ IVAN
A27. What happens when joy is unconfined—or unrefined. ~ REVEL
A29. A lock maker. ~ CURL
A30. Whose fiddle is famed in history. ~ NEROS
A32. First name of famous character actor. ~ LON
A33. This contains information of an appetizing nature. (Fr.) ~ CARTE
A34. These are beastly sounds. ~ GROWLS
A36. This conveys fresh air from the North. ~ BOREAS
A37. What does a Scotchman become at ninety? ~ OLD
A38. This often has a kick in it. ~ TOE
A39. Something often dug up for dinner. ~ POTATO
A44. A sheik of mythology. ~ ADONIS
A49. It takes more than one of these to make a quantity or sum. ~ ITEMS
A50. A hand you love to hold. ~ PAT
A52. This is never on the level. ~ SLANT
A53. To converse without ceremony. ~ CHAT
A54. This is poison to the people of India. ~ COBRA
A56. To distribute in portions. ~ DOLE
A57. What tennis champs fight over. ~ NET
A58. This has a lot of pull. ~ TOW
A59. And the rest. (Abbr.) ~ ETC
A61. One way of arranging a get-together. ~ SEW
A62. Irreverent roosters. (Abbr.) ~ IR
A63. This is often found on the watch. ~ TIME
A64. A teeny, weeny bit of matter. ~ ATOM
A66. A note in the musical scale. ~ TI
A67. A very common tube. ~ INNER
A68. These kind of roofs need no shingles. ~ TILED
A70. What an only son in a large family must have. ~ SISTERS
A71. What is the Babe doing soon after he makes a big hit? ~ SCORING

D1. A girl must have patients to be doing this. ~ NURSING
D2. First and last letter of a salt-water fish ~ CD
D3. A sheepish little one. ~ KID
D4. Girl's name. ~ INEZ
D5. When Judge Jr. refuses champagne. ~ NEVER
D6. This is often on the road. ~ GRAVEL
D7. To make less shallow. ~ DEEPEN
D8. A famous chorus. ~ ANVIL
D9. Let it stand. (Latin.) ~ STET
D10. Feminine pronoun. ~ HER
D11. If you solved Horizontal 62—this will be easy. ~ IR
D12. He who does this takes a chance. ~ GAMBLES
D16. A wandering sea-dog. ~ ROVER
D19. The great artery. ~ AORTA
D21. Polynesian plant. ~ TARO
D24. This means "to be certain." ~ SURE
D26. The present. ~ NOW
D28. This has a lot of leaves. (Abbr.) ~ VOL
D29. This runs best when tired. ~ CAR
D31. These take the pennies. ~ SLOTS
D33. Campus eye-openers. ~ COEDS
D35. A warning from the car ahead. ~ SLO
D36. A snake that embraces its opportunities. ~ BOA
D39. Parties all the bugs attend. ~ PICNICS
D40. A pronoun meaning a different person or thing. ~ OTHER
D41. This delivers milk. ~ TEAT
D42. A sum total of numbers. (Abbr.) ~ AMT
D43. One thing you get at a banquet. ~ GAB
D45. What was Methuselah? ~ OLD
D46. The principal chamber or body of a temple. (Gr., (You better work on the horizontals.) ~ NAOS
D47. A place of entrance. ~ INLET
D48. Simmering. ~ STEWING
D50. Forces. ~ POWERS
D51. Many of these were freely set up during pre-prohibition days. ~ TREATS
D54. One who approaches. ~ COMER
D55. This is always roofed over. ~ ATTIC
D58. One of a set of teeth or points. ~ TINE
D60. A Western state. (Abbr.) ~ COLO
D63. This causes noisy upheavals. ~ TNT
D65. Sea. (Fr.) ~ MER
D67. Part of the verb "to be." ~ IS
D69. Disheveled Iberians. (Abbr.) ~ DI


